            <ArticleTitle>Clinical inquiry: does topical diclofenac relieve osteoarthritis pain?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>124-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Topical diclofenac, with and without dimethyl sulfoxide (DMSO), modestly improves pain and function scores (by 4%-8%) for as long as 12 weeks in patients with osteoarthritis (OA) of the knee.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
